  "goodToKnow": "Der Hirte (die Hirtin) is a shepherd or herdsman: Schafhirte, Kuhhirte. Der Schäfer specifically herds sheep, giving der Deutsche Schäferhund (German shepherd dog). In Christian language, der gute Hirte is Jesus, and priests are Seelenhirten (shepherds of souls). Hirten appear in the Christmas story and in nativity scenes (Krippen). It's a weak noun: den Hirten. Plural: die Hirten."
